+// The dock BODY: one requestAnimationFrame steps every moving quantity of one dock.
+//
+// A lane is a keyframes `SpringProgress` stepped by `tickDt` from this loop; the
+// spring's own `.play()` loop is never started. The loop runs only while a lane is
+// moving and parks when every lane has seated, so an idle dock requests no frames.
+//
+// Two lane kinds:
+//   - `spatial` lanes are built `respectReducedMotion: true`: under reduced motion a
+//     retarget seats in the frame it is made (canon P6 drops the transform).
+//   - `fade` lanes are built `false`: they keep their curve under reduced motion
+//     (canon P6 keeps the fade).
+//
+// Landing, on the dock rung (no `dampingFraction` given). A lane LANDS on the first frame
+// its step ends within `eps` of its target: it paints that value, and seats on the target
+// the next frame, so the last step into the target is at most `eps`, never `eps` plus a
+// frame of motion. At ζ 0.88 the approach is monotone until the crossing, and the rung's
+// 0.3 %-of-travel overshoot is undesigned: it would paint as a sub-pixel settle ring
+// (O-64 R-3), so it never paints. A step that crosses its target and ends inside the band
+// seats on the target too.
+//
+// Landing, with a designed damping (`dampingFraction` given, REGISTRY §5 Q-5 (b)). The
+// overshoot is the design, so the band is no landing: the lane seats only at rest,
+// within `eps` of its target and slower than `eps` per 60 Hz frame. The lane passes
+// through the band on its way to the peak and paints the bounce.
+//
+// Time. `dt` is frame time: the rAF timestamp, measured from the frame the trigger
+// landed in (`document.timeline.currentTime` at the kick), so each step is the interval
+// between the frames that paint it, however late the main thread runs a frame's
+// callbacks. It is capped at two 60 Hz frames, so a stalled morph resumes where it
+// froze; a timestamp from before the stall (Chromium hands one to the first callback
+// after a long task) steps 0.
+
+import { SpringProgress } from "@mkbabb/keyframes.js";
+import { inject, onScopeDispose, provide, type InjectionKey } from "vue";
+
+import { motionTempo } from "../../../composables/motion/core/motionTempo";
+import { DOCK_SPRING } from "../constants";
+
+/** The longest step the body takes, ms: two 60 Hz frames. */
+export const DOCK_BODY_MAX_DT_MS = 1000 / 30;
+
+export type DockLaneKind = "spatial" | "fade";
+
+export interface DockLaneOptions {
+    kind: DockLaneKind;
