+// THE MEASURED SCENE [D2-B′]. One model of the dock in layout space, one trigger per
+// fact, and every morph as FLIP on the dock's one body (useDockBody).
+//
+// The model. In the root's own px:
+//   - the plate's four edges and its corner radius;
+//   - the regions (leading `.dock-persistent`, `.dock-layers`, trailing `.dock-persistent`);
+//   - the faces (the full face, which is the run, and the summary), inside `.dock-layers`;
+//   - the cells (each face's flex items, read through `display: contents`), inside their
+//     face, and the seats of a crossfade inside a cell, inside that cell.
+// Sizes are the used border boxes from computed style. Positions are layout
+// (`offsetLeft`/`offsetTop` summed up to the frame), never a `getBoundingClientRect()`:
+// an ancestor scale or rotate never enters the model.
+//
+// The episode. On a trigger the scene reads the new layout (Last). Every quantity's lane
+// holds `painted − layout`, so First is the lane's current value re-expressed against
+// Last, and each lane carries it to 0 on the dock rung with the velocity it already had.
+// A posture morph moves the plate and the regions; cells move only when their place
+// inside their face changes (a content change, compaction), so a posture morph writes no
+// cell. A leaving face rides its region like the current one and fades out on the
+// crossfade; a seat that leaves the compact rung holds the place it was painted at and
+// fades.
+//
+// Content appears as the glass reaches it: a seat's opacity is its coverage, 1 when it
+// sits 4 px or more inside the plate's current rect and 0 when any part is outside,
+// linear between, times the seat's own opacity (a disabled seat's dim). Nothing paints
+// beyond the glass and nothing is cut mid-glyph. A seat
+// that joins mid-life appears as its neighbours make room: its opacity is also its
+// clearance, 1 when no sibling's painted box overlaps it and 0 at 4 px of overlap.
+//
+// The window. `[data-morphing]` is up while any spatial lane travels: it opens with the
+// episode and closes on the frame the last spatial lane lands (within 0.5 px). Fades may
+// keep painting after it.
+//
+// Triggers (one per fact):
